{"title":"2013 USAJMO Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find all real numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/6/1661ee6ba75b1df39577c967cb0f537cc66e97af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,y,z\\geq 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"77\" height=\"15\" /> satisfying <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26edbd87f49eb68ec9b662b602db712e5151dc9c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\min(\\sqrt{x+xyz},\\sqrt{y+xyz},\\sqrt{z+xyz})=\\sqrt{x-1}+\\sqrt{y-1}+\\sqrt{z-1}.\\]\" width=\"516\" height=\"22\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_with_Thought_Process\">Solution with Thought Process</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution with Thought Process\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Without loss of generality, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/6/d866d8b18b69681bace25734ce9b181cb4c91a34.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\le x \\le y \\le z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"110\" height=\"15\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/5/c05abdae1dde79bcf35d5857a559fd1c626becde.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{x + xyz} = \\sqrt{x - 1} + \\sqrt{y - 1} + \\sqrt{z - 1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"317\" height=\"22\" />.\n</p><p>Suppose x = y = z. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/e/ece181b362367d6a2f19ffeea68c93271cfeb4a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{x + x^3} = 3\\sqrt{x-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"156\" height=\"19\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/6/f9661cd78041f3f76b20b39f3500db27dcf6cacc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + x^3 = 9x - 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"125\" height=\"16\" />. It is easily verified that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/c/dbc76d1e038d0b3374666465d21084f9285eefa9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^3 - 8x + 9 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"126\" height=\"18\" /> has no solution in positive numbers greater than 1. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/b/dab7da6c690a65c7761d462a580e55024d0cbf30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{x + xyz} \\ge \\sqrt{x - 1} + \\sqrt{y - 1} + \\sqrt{z - 1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"317\" height=\"22\" /> for x = y = z. We suspect if the inequality always holds.\n</p><p>Let x = 1. Then we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/b/06be397c8093f1ba6818b7f47d0ac90de686bdc0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{1 + yz} \\ge \\sqrt{y-1} + \\sqrt{z-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"229\" height=\"22\" />, which simplifies to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/e/15ea895126a2309ec5d0795354dac079c7cc25f3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1 + yz \\ge y + z - 2 + 2\\sqrt{(y-1)(z-1)}\\]\" width=\"304\" height=\"32\" /> and hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/e/39eb443cc2a760eb03d2d95bfabdb1123da6759f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[yz - y - z + 3 \\ge 2\\sqrt{(y-1)(z-1)}\\]\" width=\"274\" height=\"32\" /> Let us try a few examples: if y = z = 2, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/c/a4c66892d0049bcc06c0668da7a7adf3a0efe61e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 &gt; 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" />; if y = z, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/5/ac585c499126cfb23c3b58ea49d6f0a0231bc66d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y^2 - 2y + 3 \\ge 2(y-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"179\" height=\"21\" />, which reduces to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/c/33cabbacfcace66b57cd1d6e83be446dd80e5d05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y^2 - 4y + 5 \\ge 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"122\" height=\"18\" />. The discriminant (16 - 20) is negative, so in fact the inequality is strict. Now notice that yz - y - z + 3 = (y-1)(z-1) + 2. Now we see we can let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/d/c5da2358c39fd189760ecb5b5bccbe107ff415dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u = \\sqrt{(y-1)(z-1)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"162\" height=\"32\" />! Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/b/34bc0d41229e722d449cac8de681088b1eb6691d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[u^2 - 2u + 2 = (u-1)^2 + 1 &gt; 0\\]\" width=\"242\" height=\"19\" /> and the claim holds for x = 1.\n</p><p>If x &gt; 1, we see the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/0/4c00be84ff63c076190ad65ee1da0b295d777748.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{x - 1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"57\" height=\"18\" /> will provide a huge obstacle when squaring. But, using the identity <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/0/3e093416d6f5ea44042c370a56e44a4cc3c0d30b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x+y+z)^2 = x^2 + y^2 + z^2 + xy + yz + xz$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"340\" height=\"19\" />:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/a/9ca4391efb211202afb93d416503511aee16aeca.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x + xyz \\ge x - 1 + y - 1 + z - 1 + 2\\sqrt{(x-1)(y-1)} + 2\\sqrt{(y-1)(z-1)} + 2\\sqrt{(x-1)(y-1)}\\]\" width=\"659\" height=\"32\" />\nwhich leads to\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/3/203dc435bb009fd94b759d273476a2c6b3a0b1da.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[xyz \\ge y + z - 3 + 2\\sqrt{(x-1)(y-1)} + 2\\sqrt{(y-1)(z-1)} + 2\\sqrt{(x-1)(z-1)}\\]\" width=\"563\" height=\"32\" />\nAgain, we experiment. If x = 2, y = 3, and z = 3, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/3/a73064211a12ff3ad4e57204a5e5b9e44ee15e7a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18 &gt; 7 + 4\\sqrt{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"109\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>Now, we see the finish: setting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/e/d9eb86d3242e9a5551db22ea0c72899ec1250d75.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u = \\sqrt{x-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"92\" height=\"18\" /> gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/2/bd2194ee3112824ab672f832ba150d7647d9fa30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = u^2 + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"82\" height=\"16\" />. We can solve a quadratic in u! Because this problem is a #6, the crown jewel of USAJMO problems, we do not hesitate in computing the messy computations:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/a/bba13029b17812c8252f321e828e1905af983f89.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[u^2(yz) - u(2\\sqrt{y-1} + 2\\sqrt{z-1}) + (3 + yz - y - z - 2\\sqrt{(y-1)(z-1)}) \\ge 0\\]\" width=\"536\" height=\"32\" />\n</p><p>Because the coefficient of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/d/eed4e78c159daecbdd4f9cac855467ffd2cab7ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u^2$\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> is positive, all we need to do is to verify that the discriminant is nonpositive:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/d/9fdfdde4a15f73872fbe1f6c1f1fdedcf88fb796.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[b^2 - 4ac = 4(y-1) + 4(z-1) - 8\\sqrt{(y-1)(z-1)} - yz(12 + 4yz - 4y - 4z - 8\\sqrt{(y-1)(z-1)})\\]\" width=\"678\" height=\"32\" />\n</p><p>Let us try a few examples. If y = z, then the discriminant D = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/a/47a2eedc13b950b43cb0919bfc9dc55755f936e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8(y-1) - 8(y-1) - yz(12 + 4y^2 - 8y - 8(y-1)) = -yz(4y^2 - 16y + 20) = -4yz(y^2 - 4y + 5) &lt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"789\" height=\"19\" />.\n</p><p>We are almost done, but we need to find the correct argument. (How frustrating!)\nSuccess! The discriminant is negative. Thus, we can replace our claim with a strict one, and there are no real solutions to the original equation in the hypothesis.\n</p><p>--Thinking Process by suli\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017233128\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.013 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.021 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 90/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 5487/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:12600:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017233128 and revision id 61854. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}